## Release versioning proposal

For a future research snapshot, use an immutable annotated tag named
`e99-research-YYYY-MM-DD-audit-N`, with the date and `N` copied from the exact
`state_version`. For example, this snapshot would be `e99-research-2026-10-10-audit-234`.
The tag annotation should record the commit, tree, state version, validation commands,
and the fact that Level I is open. This is a repository-state label, not a claim of
semantic versioning, publication, or external mathematical review. Do not retag an
existing snapshot; create no tag without repository-owner authorization.

## Readiness assessment

This commit is a reproducible **mechanical baseline** when the recorded checks pass.
The theorem-state checker verifies only registered IDs, edges, lifecycle rules, and
generated metadata. Its graph does not enumerate every lemma inside the active route
modules. Passing tests and finite certificates do not verify proofs or settle E99; an
independent mathematical audit remains necessary. Public-release clearance, licensing,
and the disposition of historical or third-party material are separate review gates.

## Independent integration replay (2026-10-14)

The integration worker independently reran the seven historical stages against a clean
worktree at the recorded commit: **7/7 passed**, including **94/94 certificates**, 22
state-tooling tests and 65 research tests. The certificate phase took 327.6 seconds.
The historical inventory and all SHA-256 records above were checked against the recorded
Git tree. This is additional mechanical evidence and does not independently audit proofs.

Current integration uses the exact-version [verification lock](../../tools/requirements-verification.lock)
and CPython 3.14.7. The baseline utility now compares every tracked working-file blob
against the commit, rejects noncache ignored inputs, and isolates Python bytecode lookup;
Git's status alone can hide edits marked assume-unchanged. On integrated checkouts it
also runs the platform integrity command. Historical checkouts retain the seven stages.
See [current verification instructions](CI.md). Historical hashes stay pinned and do not
claim byte identity for integration or a curated export.
